        "answer": "d",
        "explanation": "A tenant restriction works because the gateway adds a header naming the allowed workspaces and the service refuses any other account; it needs TLS inspection so the gateway can add the header. A URL category rule decides who may reach the hostname, but a private and a company account use the same hostname, so it cannot tell them apart. A DNS rule has the same blind spot one layer lower. A consent policy governs apps that connect to company data through OAuth, not which account a person signs in with on an outside website."
