        "answer": "b",
        "explanation": "The span with no parent is the root span, and it marks the beginning and end of the entire operation. A loose span is the opposite case: it does carry a parent_id, but the span it points at is missing from the store. Siblings are spans that share the same parent, which is unrelated to an empty parent field. Errors are shown by span status Error, not by the parent field."
